From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:48:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] settings: stop warning that "ghostty" is an unrecognised
 engine

Profile::LayerJson decided "unrecognised" by comparing the raw JSON
string against a hardcoded "cascadia", so the list of known engines
existed in two places: the JSON mapper, and that string. The day the
ghostty engine shipped, every ghostty profile told the user its engine
was not recognised while quietly working correctly.

The check now asks the mapper (IsKnownName reads the same `mappings`
FromJson does), so there is one list.

The existing test kept passing throughout, because it used "ghostty" as
its example of an *unknown* engine - it was asserting the bug. It now
uses a genuinely bogus value, and asserts that "ghostty" parses.

Added ProfileKnownEngineDoesNotWarn for the case that was missing
entirely: a shipping engine must load silently. Mutation-verified -
restoring the hardcoded comparison fails it.

unitSettingsModel: 159/159.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ee27Fih3vSPYsqrUBpUoc
